// ── THE HEADLINE WAS THE BUG ─────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// This screen said "Booking confirmed. Your stay at The Riverside Apartment is
// confirmed." with a tick, a reference of GOS-88219-X and dates of 12 to 14
// July. All fixed text, shown to everybody.
//
// The reference and the dates being invented is the ordinary Stitch problem.
// The headline is not, because most bookings are NOT confirmed at this point.
//
// A host chooses their booking mode. Where it is `request` — the default in
// BookingMode.from, so also what a misconfigured listing gets —
// createStayBooking returns status `pending` and the host has 24 hours to
// accept or decline. Telling that guest "Booking confirmed" is not a cosmetic
// inaccuracy. It is the kind that puts somebody on a train to Whitby for a
// stay nobody has agreed to.
//
// So the headline now follows the status the server actually returned, and the
// screen watches the booking: if the host accepts while the guest is still
// looking at it, it changes in front of them.
//
// ── NO PAYMENT, STILL ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// Nothing was charged on the previous screen, so nothing is receipted here.
// The next-steps list says what genuinely happens next, which for a confirmed
// stay is the arrival photographs — the evidence that protects the guest
// against a deposit claim, and the one thing they must not skip.
